  "name": "beleriand",
  "provenance": "Hand-transcribed from the project's own rulebook, BeleriandInstruction.docx. The rulebook carries no adjacency table or map image, so the province set, names and every textual geometry fact come from the rulebook (abbreviation table; Areas list; off-map box adjacencies; Ulmo's coastal-province list; Angband/Eriador clauses; the fortress list; every adjacency exercised by a rulebook example order, e.g. Gel-Hig, Tha-MMa, Hid-Hig, NLa-Lam, FoR-NEB, Est-NEB, NOs-NEB, FSi-FoR, FoB-Tal, MSi-SEB, And-SEB), and the remaining edges, terrain and neutral supply centers are an original reconstruction from the rulebook's literary source geography (Tolkien's First Age map of Beleriand). Ossiriand's starting units are absent from the rulebook and pinned as A(NOs), A(MOs), A(SOs). No other engine's data files were consulted or converted. The reconstructed army/fleet adjacency was subsequently corrected against the author's drawn board, and ELO/CNI terrain was reclassified. The mountain_barriers key holds ordered [from, to] pairs — 84 directed crossings over 78 undirected edges, an author ruling that deliberately diverges from the rulebook's symmetric 'Mountain Barriers' reading and supersedes the earlier 24-pair set.",
